  <section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-12 prose dark:prose-invert text-slate-300">
    <div class="border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800/80 pt-12 space-y-12">
      
      <!-- H2 1: Complete Privacy -->
      <div class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
          Complete Privacy: A 100% Client-Side Private Text Deduplicator
        </h2>
        <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
          Modern list hygiene frequently involves highly sensitive datasets—including customer email newsletter rosters, unreleased product SKUs, internal server URLs, and proprietary database records. Typical online text utilities quietly transmit your clipboard data over HTTP POST requests to remote cloud instances for processing, introducing compliance violations under GDPR, CCPA, and enterprise confidentiality policies.
        </p>
        <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
          FastToolVerse operates on a zero-compromise architectural standard: <strong>100% of text processing executes exclusively in your browser's local sandbox memory</strong>. No bytes are ever transmitted over the network, no cookies track your data, and no server logs are created. You can verify this by inspecting the browser Network tab or by disconnecting your internet connection entirely after loading the page.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- H2 2: Algorithmic Architecture -->
      <div class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
          High-Performance O(N) Hash Set Architecture vs Quadratic Filtering
        </h2>
        <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
          Naive text deduplication implementations rely on nested loops or <code class="text-xs font-mono bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-purple-600 dark:text-purple-400">Array.prototype.indexOf()</code> / <code class="text-xs font-mono bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-purple-600 dark:text-purple-400">Array.prototype.filter()</code>. In algorithmic terms, scanning an entire array for every single element introduces quadratic time complexity—<strong>O(N&sup2;)</strong>. When processing a dataset of 50,000 lines, a quadratic algorithm requires up to 2.5 billion comparison operations, inevitably freezing the browser thread and displaying a "Page Unresponsive" dialog.
        </p>
        <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
          FastToolVerse utilizes modern ECMAScript <strong>Hash Sets (<code class="text-xs font-mono bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-purple-600 dark:text-purple-400">new Set()</code>)</strong>. Hash sets provide near-instantaneous <strong>O(1)</strong> lookup and insertion complexity:
        </p>
        
        <div class="not-prose my-4 p-4 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 bg-slate-950 font-mono text-xs text-purple-300 overflow-x-auto space-y-2">
          <div><span class="text-slate-500">// High-performance linear O(N) deduplication loop</span></div>
          <div>const seen = new Set();</div>
          <div>const uniqueLines = [];</div>
          <div class="pt-1">for (let i = 0; i &lt; lines.length; i++) &#123;</div>
          <div class="pl-4">let line = trimWhitespace ? lines[i].trim() : lines[i];</div>
          <div class="pl-4">if (removeEmpty &amp;&amp; !line) continue;</div>
          <div class="pl-4">const key = caseSensitive ? line : line.toLowerCase();</div>
          <div class="pl-4">if (!seen.has(key)) &#123;</div>
          <div class="pl-8">seen.add(key);</div>
          <div class="pl-8">uniqueLines.push(line); <span class="text-slate-500">// Preserves first occurrence order</span></div>
          <div class="pl-4">&#125;</div>
          <div>&#125;</div>
        </div>

        <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
          This linear <strong>O(N)</strong> architecture processes datasets containing 50,000+ entries in under 40 milliseconds, ensuring smooth, instantaneous responsiveness as you type, adjust checkboxes, or paste massive datasets.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- H2 3: How Whitespace and Case Sensitivity Affect Deduplication -->
      <div class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
          How Whitespace Normalization &amp; Case Sensitivity Prevent False Positives
        </h2>
        <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
          In real-world data, duplicates rarely appear with byte-for-byte identical formatting. Three common hidden variables prevent naive deduplicators from catching duplicates:
        </p>
        <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm sm:text-base text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 list-disc pl-5">
          <li><strong>Hidden Whitespace &amp; Trailing Tabs:</strong> Copying rows from spreadsheets often attaches an invisible trailing tab (<code class="text-xs font-mono bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-purple-600 dark:text-purple-400">\t</code>) or trailing space to some rows. Enabling <em>Trim whitespace before comparing</em> normalizes each line before hashing, ensuring phantom spaces don't bypass duplicate detection.</li>
          <li><strong>Letter Casing Discrepancies:</strong> In CRM lists, email addresses often enter with mixed capitalization (e.g., <code class="text-xs font-mono bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-purple-600 dark:text-purple-400">User@Domain.com</code> vs <code class="text-xs font-mono bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-purple-600 dark:text-purple-400">user@domain.com</code>). In case-insensitive mode, the internal comparison key is lowered, eliminating duplicate messages while preserving the clean capitalization of the first appearance.</li>
          <li><strong>Repetitive Blank Rows:</strong> Disjointed documents often separate sections with erratic sequences of blank lines. When <em>Remove empty/blank lines</em> is checked, all empty and whitespace-only lines are purged completely; when unchecked, only the first blank line is kept while repeated blank lines are cleaned.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <!-- H2 4: Real-World Use Cases -->
      <div class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
          Practical Industry Applications: From Digital Marketing to Data Engineering
        </h2>
        <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
          Deduplicating lists is a fundamental workflow step across multiple technological domains:
        </p>
        <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm sm:text-base text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 list-disc pl-5">
          <li><strong>SEO &amp; Content Strategy:</strong> Cleaning aggregated keyword exports from Google Search Console, Ahrefs, or Semrush to prevent targeting cannibalization across search campaigns.</li>
          <li><strong>Email Deliverability &amp; CRM:</strong> Deduplicating newsletter subscriber lists before sending email blasts via Mailchimp, Klaviyo, or SendGrid to avoid double messaging and improve sender reputation scores.</li>
          <li><strong>Web Crawling &amp; Sitemap Audits:</strong> Sanitizing lists of extracted URLs, internal redirect chains, and canonical link targets before submitting sitemaps to search engines.</li>
          <li><strong>Database &amp; Spreadsheet Sanitization:</strong> Cleaning pasted single-column exports of order numbers, customer IDs, and inventory SKUs before executing SQL queries or Excel <code class="text-xs font-mono bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-purple-600 dark:text-purple-400">VLOOKUP</code> routines.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- FAQ Section (SEO crawlable) -->
  <section class="py-16 sm:py-24">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      
      <div class="text-center mb-12">
        <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
          Frequently Asked Questions
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm sm:text-base text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
          Everything you need to know about client-side text deduplication, privacy, and algorithms.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Semantic FAQ List -->
      <div class="space-y-4">
        {faqs.map((faq) => (
          <details class="group rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 p-5 transition-all duration-200 open:shadow-xs">
            <summary class="flex items-center justify-between font-semibold text-sm sm:text-base text-slate-900 dark:text-white cursor-pointer list-none select-none">
